[E-INSTANCE-NONE] Error: no `DecEq` instance for `Box`
    ╭─[ soundness/quot-derive-eq.sw:13:28 ]
    │
 13 │ def same (b: Box): Bool := b == b
    │                            ───┬──  
    │                               ╰──── this needs `DecEq Box`
    │ 
    │ Note 1: `==` isn't derived for `Box`: its field `q` has type `Quot Bool AllTrue`, which has no `DecEq` instance (when `Box` was declared); a quotient has no `==` unless one is written for it: comparing the values two quotients were made from could call equal quotients different; to give one `==`, wrap it in a record (`type Q = { raw: Quot … }`) and declare a `DecEq` instance for the record
    │ 
    │ Note 2: an instance of `DecEq` for `Box` can be declared in `Main`
────╯
